<!--
  PRODUCT_SPEC PLAY-002 — a side-profile car for the Android Auto action slot, which is tiny.

  Drawn to three rules a 24dp slot enforces, all of which the previous glyph broke and a device run saw:

  - **Centred on both axes.** The glyph spans y 6→18.5 and is symmetric about x=12. The earlier path sat
    between y 5 and 17 and left the bottom third of the box empty, so the car floated above the middle of
    a slot the host centres its other icons in.
  - **Wheels under the ends of the body.** They sit at x 7.1 and 16.9 inside a body spanning 2.6→21.4. The
    earlier front wheel was at 15.2 under a body reaching 22.3, a seven-unit overhang that read as a
    misplaced wheel rather than a nose.
  - **No detail that cannot survive the size.** One silhouette: body, cabin, two wheels, no window and no
    bumper spur. Each wheel keeps about seven-tenths of its circle below the body edge, which is what makes
    it read as a wheel instead of a flat stub at 24dp.

  The cabin sits back over the rear axle rather than in the middle. That asymmetry is what makes the shape
  a car instead of a shed, and it costs nothing: the *glyph* stays centred, only its interior is weighted.
-->
